[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: Rebind all pseudo-state-machine transition overrides to the contract operation types from low/semver_solver.pyi (Version, VersionEngine, PackageRepository, DependencySolver) instead of the concrete impl classes, so every override shadows its inherited interface transition during real-SUT execution. Added Version.format and name-bound is_prerelease overrides that call_target the real Version, exposed a real Version instance through SemverSolverSUT and TestSemverSolverImplReal.setUp (singletons/checked bindings keyed by contract types), and asserted real canonical formatting/is_prerelease behavior. Overrides now return the real compare_precedence, satisfies, and resolve results so contracted prerelease ordering, range matching, and real derivation steps are validated instead of the fixed fake-model oracles.
[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_pretense.py: The state-machine model transitions contradict low/semver_solver.pyi and are used as the oracle for the real SUT, so contract-correct implementation results are rejected. compare_precedence at lines 159-166 compares only numeric core equality and order, so it returns a positive ordering for Version(1,0,0,('alpha','1')) versus Version(1,0,0) instead of the required negative ranking of a prerelease below its normal release, and it never applies numeric versus ASCII prerelease identifier comparison, the numeric-below-string rule, or the longer-sequence rule. satisfies at lines 193-195 ignores the range entirely, returning True for Version(0,0,0) against VersionRange('^1.0.0') and for prerelease candidates whenever include_prerelease is True, whereas the contract requires comparator-boundary evaluation and the explicit prerelease-targeting exception. resolve at lines 257-262 hardcodes the selected versions and the literal derivation-steps tuple regardless of the registered repository state, whereas the contract requires the highest mutually compatible assignment and an ordered sequence of decision and deduction steps. format at lines 130-133 strips build metadata, so it cannot produce the canonical SemVer string for versions carrying build identifiers. The model must compute the contracted precedence, range satisfaction, and state-derived resolution outcome rather than fixed fake values.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_pretense.py: Replaced fixed fake oracles with contract-correct model algebra: full SemVer 2.0.0 precedence (numeric core ordering, prerelease-below-normal, numeric-vs-ASCII identifiers, numeric-below-string, longer-sequence rule), real range satisfaction (comparator boundaries, caret/tilde/wildcard/hyphen/union expansion, numeric boundary shifting, and the explicit prerelease-targeting exception vs include_prerelease filtering), canonical formatting that preserves build metadata, and a state-derived resolution outcome that selects the highest compatible registered release per dependency with ordered decision steps (including transitive dependencies). parse_version/parse_range now genuinely derive records from input text. Expanded the fixed fake test to exercise build formatting, prerelease precedence, ^1.0.0 boundary rejection, and state-derived resolution.
