[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_pretense.py: Resolve model no longer imposes its own derivation-step wording: it still derives the highest compatible selected_versions mapping and ordered decision steps from registered state, but validates only the selected_versions mapping and the ordered step count (len(ret.derivation_steps) == len(steps)) instead of asserting full ResolutionOutcome equality against synthesized step strings. Also stabilized the modeled Version: SemverSolverState now carries an explicit model version used by format (canonical string including build metadata) and is_prerelease, so the version formatted by the model and the Version bound into real fixtures can be kept identical, with parse_version continuing to record parsed history. Fake scenarios cover default, build-metadata, and prerelease formatting.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: Keep the real-SUT fixture's Version consistent with the state-machine model: TestSemverSolverImplReal.setUp and the prerelease fixture now construct the pseudo state machine with SemverSolverState(version=<bound Version>), so the inherited format/is_prerelease model and the bound real Version describe the same version. SemverSolverSUT now exposes the same model default Version(0,0,0) that the fuzz initial state records, so format and is_prerelease agree with the model throughout fuzzing; build/prerelease formatting coverage stays in the interface fake scenarios.
