[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: The expanded deterministic suite improves coverage but still leaves contracted low-level behavior unexercised, so the residual gap is a specification gap. parse_range must be exercised for comparator targets with more than three numeric components, a numeric component after a wildcard, leading zeroes in numeric and prerelease identifiers, malformed prerelease and build identifiers, build metadata carried on a comparator target, prerelease or build metadata combined with a wildcard, an operator separated from its target by whitespace as explicitly permitted (for example '>= 1.0.0'), an operator with no target, and a hyphen separator that does not form a complete hyphen range, each of which must either parse under the contracted grammar or raise InvalidRangeError. satisfies must be exercised for exact equality targets, standalone and partial wildcards combined with every relational operator including the universal wildcard that must match no version, exclusion of a standalone universal wildcard, hyphen ranges whose upper bound is a wildcard, caret and tilde prefixes whose boundaries are determined by all-zero or wildcard minor and patch components, and prerelease filtering where a prerelease candidate satisfies the numeric boundaries while no boundary carries a prerelease identifier, which must evaluate to False when include_prerelease is False. compare_precedence must be exercised for a normal version ordered above a prerelease sharing the same numeric core and for equal prerelease sequences with matching numeric identifiers. resolve must be exercised for forward checking where a candidate release declares a dependency on an already-assigned package whose assigned version violates the dependency range, forcing backtracking and, when no compatible assignment exists, a ResolutionConflictError carrying derivation detail.
[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver_impl.py: Lines 81 and 309 are unreachable defensive guards: version specifier text and clause token lists reach the parser only as non-empty whitespace-split tokens of a non-empty clause, so an empty specifier or empty token list cannot occur under the contracted grammar. Line 159 is unreachable because the wildcard upper-bound computation is invoked only for specifiers that retain at least one wildcard component, so the all-numeric branch can never execute. Lines 380 and 385 are unreachable because the only expanded comparators that omit a lower or upper boundary are the universal-wildcard false comparator and the wildcard-exclusion comparator, both fully handled by the preceding branches, so the unbounded-comparator fallbacks can never execute. Prune these lines or mark them with pretense.unreachable() or '# pragma: no cover (assumption: specifier tokens are non-empty and wildcard comparators always carry their boundaries)'.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: Closed the remaining specification-coverage gaps in TestSemverSolverImplReal: new test_parse_range_edge_cases exercises >3-component comparator targets, a numeric component after a wildcard, leading zeroes in numeric/prerelease identifiers, malformed prerelease/build identifiers, build metadata on comparator targets, prerelease/build metadata on wildcards, whitespace-separated operator (>= 1.0.0, asserted to parse and satisfy), operator-without-target, and incomplete hyphen separators (each parsing under the grammar or raising InvalidRangeError, with raw_text trimming asserted when parsed). New test_satisfies_equality_and_wildcards covers exact = and == equality, standalone universal wildcard and its relational forms (=*, >=*, <=*, >*, <*, !=*) including the wildcard that matches no version and the excluded universal wildcard, partial wildcards across every relational operator (>=1.x, >1.x, <1.x, <=1.x, !=1.x), hyphen ranges with a wildcard upper bound, caret/tilde boundaries driven by all-zero or wildcard minor/patch (^0.x, ^0.0.x, ~0.x, ~0.0.x), and prerelease filtering where numeric boundaries are met but no boundary carries a prerelease identifier. compare_precedence now also asserts normal-above-prerelease for the same core and equality of matching prerelease sequences. New test_resolution_forward_checking exercises a candidate release whose declared dependency violates an already-assigned package (forcing backtracking to a compatible assignment) and the unsatisfiable variant that raises ResolutionConflictError with conflicting packages and derivation explanation.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver_impl.py: Resolved unreachable-code feedback: pruned the empty specifier/empty clause guards, removed the all-numeric wildcard upper-bound branch, and refactored expanded comparators to always carry concrete lower and upper boundaries (unsatisfiable wildcard uses a sentinel), eliminating the unbounded-comparator fallbacks. Static checks pass.
[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver_impl.py: The universal-wildcard negation is mishandled, violating the satisfies postcondition in low/semver_solver.pyi that a candidate must evaluate True only when it satisfies the range and False otherwise. The wildcard-exclusion expansion in _wildcard_exclude_items at lines 208-214 returns an empty comparator clause whenever the excluded specifier has no finite lower or upper boundary; for VersionRange('!=*') both boundaries are None, so it produces an empty clause, and an empty clause is vacuously satisfied by every candidate, making satisfies(Version(1,2,3), VersionRange('!=*'), False) return True. Since the universal wildcard admits every precedence ordering, its negation can match no version, so the exclusion path must emit the unsatisfiable sentinel comparator already used for the sibling open-ended wildcard relational forms (the 'false' comparator used by >* and <* around lines 235-260) rather than an empty clause. The latest change added the sentinel for the open-ended comparator branches but left the wildcard-exclusion branch returning an empty clause, so the !=* assertion in test_satisfies_equality_and_wildcards still fails; the wildcard-exclusion expansion must return the sentinel comparator when either boundary is unbounded, which is exactly the universal-wildcard case.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver_impl.py: Fixed universal-wildcard negation: _wildcard_exclude_items now emits the unsatisfiable sentinel comparator when the excluded specifier has no finite boundaries (e.g. !=*), so a negated universal wildcard matches no version instead of vacuously matching everything. Audited sibling wildcard relational expansions for the same defect; !range still handles finite exclusions such as !=1.x. Static checks pass.
